# UDSINIT on the manual's AO example: element 7 is a UserDefined (influence-function deformable mirror)
# surface whose coefficients come from AOmirror.test (cmdref: Surface Data).  The deck loads the file itself
# (UDSrfParam= must precede UDSrfFile= -- the example had them the other way round and its ten UDSrfParam
# values split over two lines until 2026-10-16, which printed a parse warning and an "Unidentified string");
# UDSINIT re-reads the same file and the exit-pupil OPD is unchanged.
cd $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples
old AOExample.in
opd 16
/null
udsinit
7
AOmirror.test
opd 16
# EXPECT: RMS OPD error is\s+3\.1638\d*D-07[\s\S]*?Enter user-defined surface file name \[none\]: AOmirror\.test[\s\S]*?RMS OPD error is\s+3\.1638\d*D-07
# EXPECT-NOT: Must specify UDSrfParam
# EXPECT-NOT: Unidentified string
# EXPECT-NOT: Unknown user-defined surface type
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
